From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:48:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] j604: build the J604 series on integration/aurora,
 taking Aurora's side

The J604 series was rebased from a82a1ebda940 onto integration/aurora
cc7696978e4c with Aurora's side kept in every conflicting hunk. Where
that left a file half ours and half Aurora's, take Aurora's file whole:
the core Apple SoC drivers both sides changed (RTKit, mailbox, DART,
ATC PHY, PCIe, NVMe, SMC, PMP, AIC, the SEP crate), the display driver
and the GPU driver.

Our deep-sleep bring-up is dropped for Aurora's sleep driver: the
suspend-to-RAM driver, its hooks in other drivers and our CPU hotplug
provider (Aurora's spin-table code has its own). Suspend-to-idle is
unchanged.

The Neural Engine, video encoder and camera drivers stay as the J604
series has them, since Aurora lacks their T8132 support. The camera no
longer restores the DART address filter itself: Aurora's DART replays it
when it powers up.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
